--- fetch -- HTTP client contract (WinterCG `fetch` surface).
---
--- `fetch(input, init)` resolves to a Response record; backends
--- (`fetch-c` over libcurl, `fetch-js` over the generated WebIDL
--- bindings) export a `fetch` arrow of this signature, and may also
--- expose the step-arrow form `fetch_task` for `concurrent` schedulers.
---
--- Request: `input` is the URL string; `init` fields are all optional:
---   method      "GET" default
---   headers     { name: value } record
---   body        String
---   body_bytes  Bytes
---   timeout_ms  Int
---   follow      Bool
---   user_agent  String
---   insecure    Bool (self-signed test servers only)
---
--- Response: `{ status: Int, headers: {..}, body: String,
---   body_bytes: Bytes }`; transport failure raises `err`.
---
--- `~[1]~>` marks the call effectful: every backend reaches a foreign
--- transport through `ffi.call` / `js.call`.

export Fetch     := (String, Init) ~>[1] Response
export FetchTask := (String, Init) ~>[1] Task
